<title>USA: Duquesne Pa. 833 MW nuke back this weekend.</title>
<headline>Duquesne Pa. 833 MW nuke back this weekend.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duquesne Light Co said Friday the 833 megawatt (MW) unit 2 at the Beaver Valley nuclear power plant would resume operation this weekend after it tripped off line Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We expected it to be on line this weekend,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Duquesne, a subsidiary of DQE Inc, operates and holds partial stake in the Beaver Valley unit in Shippingport, Pa.</p>
<p>Ohio Edison and Centerior Energy are the other owners of Beaver Valley 2.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
